      ],
      "source": "https://museumsdatabase.com/museums/view/21679"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Town of Western Historical Society, founded in 1958, preserves and shares the town’s rich history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://museumsdatabase.com/museums/view/21679"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Every summer, the society hosts a three‑day Westernville Heritage Days celebration on Main Street.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://museumsdatabase.com/museums/view/21679"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Swan Homestead, a historic home on Main Street, was built by Gustavus Swan and remains a landmark.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Westernville%2C_New_York"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "William Floyd House, a Revolutionary War hero’s home, is listed on the National Register of Historic Places since 1971.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
